# Render static-site _redirects rules. Top-to-bottom, first match wins.
# Rules only fire when no physical file matches the requested path.
#
# Two categories of redirects, plus the SPA fallback at the end:
#   1. /articles/<slug>           -> /articles/<slug>.html      (301)
#   2. /providers/<slug>          -> /providers/<slug>/         (301)
#   3. /*                         -> /index.html                (200)
#
# Why these exist: Google Search Console flagged "Duplicate, Google chose
# different canonical than user" and "Alternate page with proper canonical
# tag" for the extensionless / trailing-slashless variants. Without
# redirects, those bare URLs were falling through to the SPA shell and
# serving the homepage's canonical at a non-homepage URL.

